      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel disillusioned when your actions lead to such devastating personal cost. The weight of systemic corruption can feel insurmountable, making any small effort seem futile. However, your integrity is a valuable thing, and while the external world may feel broken, your personal strength remains. Focusing on finding small, manageable ways to rebuild your own life and finding a supportive community can be a start toward finding a different kind of meaningful purpose.",
      "source": "target",
